- op: discuss  # 96a4
  at: '2026-08-16T08:13:33Z'  # 96a4
  by: agent  # 96a4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 96a4
  clock: 3  # 96a4
  nonce: 96a4  # 96a4
  message: "SATISFIED — the label now names what is checked, and the overclaiming\nspelling is structurally refused.\n\nRESOLUTION CHOSEN (from the item's three candidates): rename, not a coverage\ngate. Rationale: the coverage claim already has a real, checked home —\n`module_completeness` (dated per-module audits, per-SLOT and EXACT, the\nsingle grant of confirmability per ADR-0016 as extended by PR #360) — so\nbuilding a second coverage mechanism into `status` would create one fact\nwith two homes (the exact rule-7 shape). The satisfiable claim the item\nnames (\"every I/O-performing stdlib function is listed\") is precisely what\nmodule_completeness asserts per module, with a date and a file.\n\nSHIPPED (PR pending at time of writing; will be merged by auto-pr):\n- `_validate_catalog_dict` vocabulary: {provenance_declared, in_progress}.\n  The literal `complete` RAISES with a migration-pointing error naming\n  INV-titih — the misleading spelling cannot silently return.\n- The four citation checks are unchanged under the new name (pinned by\n  test_io_boundary_status_provenance_declared.py).\n- All shipped catalogue YAMLs renamed (3 carried the live label: python,\n  rust, erlang); the 11 in_progress catalogues' \"promotion to complete\"\n  comments rewritten to state the citation-only meaning.\n- Dataclass docstring + _from_dict default + overlay-refusal message +\n  MIGRATION-IO-BOUNDARIES.md all updated; the three senses of \"complete\"\n  the item documents are now one word each: provenance_declared (citation),\n  module_completeness (dated coverage audit), and plain-English \"complete\"\n  (no longer claimable).\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN PROHIBITION honoured: the six missing os rows were NOT the\nfix here (they landed separately in PR #365 for recall reasons, before this\nitem was worked); this change fixes the CLASS — the assertion is either\nchecked or unspeakable.\n\nSEPARABLE DEFECT split out rather than folded in: load_catalog returns the\ndataclass default status for a MISSING catalogue file, which post-rename\nreads provenance_declared for uncatalogued languages. Changing it flips\ndst_classification_unreliable for catalogue-less languages, so it needs its\nown measured change; pinned as-is by\ntest_missing_catalog_default_pinned_as_is and filed as a work item.\n\nBehavioral evidence: full affected suite green on the branch; live-tree test\nloads every shipped catalogue under the new vocabulary and asserts none says\ncomplete; the refusal path is a positive test (ValueError with the\nmigration message), not an assumption."  # 96a4
